Update YAC
YAC checks GitHub using the existing internet connection.

Looking: checking for an update.
No Internet: GitHub could not be reached; returns to Settings.
No Update: no newer release; returns to Settings.
Update Found: asks Read Notes Y/N?. Whether you read or skip the notes, Update Y/N? follows.

h: read this help again.
n: skip notes at Read Notes Y/N?; decline installation and return to Settings at Update Y/N?.
q: cancel and return to Settings. During notes, q leaves only the notes.
r: read the release notes again. Long notes use Space for the next page and q to leave. Afterwards, Update Y/N? appears.
y: read notes at Read Notes Y/N?. At Update Y/N?, download, verify and install, then restart YAC.

The radio stays connected until installation begins. Saved settings are kept. Local-file installation is not available. On the Pi, separate helpers and boot setup are not updated.
